IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 2, ss 6 to 12, the Fourth
-- Schedule and the Fifth Schedule.  Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 310 to 1004
-- and 2573 to 2636.
--
-- Where a court "may", the rules answer whether the power is available on the
-- facts, never whether the court will exercise it.  Where the Act delegates to
-- regulations (ss 6(6), 9(7), 9(10), 9(12), 11) the prescribed figure is an input
-- and, where none is supplied, the Act's own figure is the law; where the Act
-- supplies no fallback (s 11) the rule is a named refusal.

§ `Part 2 -- Unfair practices: redress`

§§ `6. Consumer's right to sue for unfair practice`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(6)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `the limit prescribed by the Minister by order in the Gazette in place of $30,000`
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 30_000

-- 6(4): the annual rent, or 12 times the monthly rent.

GIVEN v IS A `Residential Valuation Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the annual rent, or 12 times the monthly rent` MEANS
    CONSIDER v's `the annual rent payable by the tenant in respect of the immovable property`
    WHEN JUST annual THEN JUST annual
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER v's `the monthly rent payable by the tenant in respect of the immovable property`
        WHEN JUST monthly THEN JUST (12 TIMES monthly)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- 6(4)(a) annual value; (b) annual rent or 12 times monthly rent, if lower than
-- (a); (c) one-tenth of the last transacted price if the annual value, annual rent
-- or monthly rent cannot be ascertained (read: none of them can; see NOTES.md F1).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(4)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN v IS A `Residential Valuation Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of residential property` MEANS
    CONSIDER v's `the annual value of the immovable property appearing in the Valuation List prepared under section 10 of the Property Tax Act 1960`
    WHEN JUST annualvalue THEN
        CONSIDER `the annual rent, or 12 times the monthly rent` v
        WHEN JUST rent THEN IF rent LESS THAN annualvalue THEN rent ELSE annualvalue
        WHEN NOTHING THEN annualvalue
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the annual rent, or 12 times the monthly rent` v
        WHEN JUST rent THEN rent
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER v's `the last transacted price`
            WHEN JUST price THEN price DIVIDED BY 10
            WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "no annual value, rent or last transacted price is given, so the value of the residential property cannot be determined under section 6(4)"

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(2)(a), (3) and (5)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount of the claim exceeds the prescribed limit` IF
        a's `the amount of the claim` GREATER THAN `the prescribed limit` a
    AND NOT (    a's `the amount claimed is a balance after a set-off admitted by the consumer in the particulars of the claim`
             AND a's `the balance after that set-off` AT MOST `the prescribed limit` a)
    AND NOT a's `the consumer has abandoned the excess over the prescribed limit`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(2)(b) and (4)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the value of the subject matter exceeds the prescribed limit` IF
    (IF a's `the subject matter is residential property`
     THEN `the value of residential property` (a's `the valuation facts of the residential property`)
     ELSE a's `the value of the subject matter, where it is not residential property`)
    GREATER THAN `the prescribed limit` a

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(1) and (2)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right to commence an action under section 6(1) does not apply` IF
    IF a's `the claim is a claim for money`
    THEN `the amount of the claim exceeds the prescribed limit` a
    ELSE `the value of the subject matter exceeds the prescribed limit` a

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(1)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` IF
        a's `the consumer has entered a consumer transaction involving an unfair practice`
    AND a's `the action is commenced in a court of competent jurisdiction against the supplier`
    AND NOT `the right to commence an action under section 6(1) does not apply` a

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(5)(b)"
GIVEN a IS A `Consumer Action Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that the consumer may recover in the action` MEANS
    IF a's `the consumer has abandoned the excess over the prescribed limit`
    THEN `the prescribed limit` a
    ELSE a's `the amount of the claim`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(7)"
GIVEN s IS A `Stay Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party may apply to stay the proceedings` IF
        s's `an application has been made under section 9 against the same supplier`
    AND s's `the proceedings relate to the unfair practice to which the application relates`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(8)"
GIVEN s IS A `Stay Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may stay the proceedings` IF
        s's `a party to the action applies for a stay`
    AND `a party may apply to stay the proceedings` s
    AND s's `the court is satisfied that the determination of the application under section 9 will be material to the action`

GIVEN s IS A `Stay Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date from which the two years run` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the date of the last further step taken by any party after the stay order`
    WHEN JUST step THEN IF step GREATER THAN s's `the stay order was made on` THEN step ELSE s's `the stay order was made on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN s's `the stay order was made on`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(9)"
GIVEN s IS A `Stay Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may of its own motion discontinue the stayed proceedings` IF
    s's `the date on which the court considers discontinuing the proceedings`
        AT LEAST `add months` (`the date from which the two years run` s) 24

§§ `7. Jurisdiction and powers of courts`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a relevant contract` IF
        t's `the contract is a contract mentioned in paragraph 1(a) or (c) of the Schedule to the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984`
    AND NOT t's `the contract relates to the sale of immovable property`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(1)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN t IS A `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` IF
    CONSIDER t's `kind of action`
    WHEN `an action under section 6(1)` THEN
            t's `the action relates to an unfair practice or an undertaking in respect of an unfair practice`
        AND `the contract is a relevant contract` t
    WHEN `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)` THEN
            t's `the action relates to an unfair practice or an undertaking in respect of an unfair practice`
        AND `the contract is a relevant contract` t
    WHEN `an action under regulations made under section 11` THEN
            `the contract is a relevant contract` t
         OR t's `the action relates to a time share contract or a time share related contract`
    WHEN `an action under provisions specified under section 43(2)(j)` THEN
            `the contract is a relevant contract` t
    WHEN `an action relating to a deposit paid in relation to or in contemplation of a motor vehicle sale contract` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other action` THEN FALSE

-- 7(4): for the District Court limit and the Magistrate's Court limit, an action
-- under s 6(1) is deemed to be a claim founded on contract.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(4)"
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is deemed a claim founded on contract for the court limits` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an action under section 6(1)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 7(9): goods or services intended for business use include goods or services the
-- consumer intends to resell, and goods the consumer intends to use up or transform.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(9)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Relief Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods or services are intended for business use` IF
        r's `the consumer intends to resell the goods or services in the course of the consumer's business`
     OR r's `the consumer intends to use up or transform the goods in the course of the consumer's business in a process of production or manufacturing or in repairing or treating other goods or fixtures`
     OR r's `the goods or services are otherwise intended for business use`

-- 7(7) and (8): no relief for business-use goods or services in an action under
-- s 6(1); the court may apportion and grant relief for the non-business portion.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(7) and (8)"
GIVEN r IS A `Relief Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share of the goods or services for which relief may be granted` MEANS
    IF `the goods or services are intended for business use` r
       AND r's `the action is an action under section 6(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER r's `the share of the goods or services attributed by the court to non-business use, where it has apportioned the use`
          WHEN JUST share THEN share
          WHEN NOTHING THEN 0)
    ELSE 1

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(5) and (7)"
GIVEN r IS A `Relief Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` IF
        NOT r's `the court is a Small Claims Tribunal`
    AND r's `the court finds that the supplier has engaged in an unfair practice`
    AND `the share of the goods or services for which relief may be granted` r GREATER THAN 0

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(5)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN r IS A `Relief Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of Relief`
`the reliefs the court may grant under section 7(5)` MEANS
    IF `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` r
    THEN LIST `restitution of money, property or other consideration given or furnished by the consumer`
              , `damages in the amount of any loss or damage suffered by the consumer`
              , `specific performance against the supplier`
              , `an order to repair goods or provide parts for goods`
              , `an order varying the contract between the supplier and the consumer`
    ELSE EMPTY

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(10)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN g IS A `Regard Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must have regard to the consumer's efforts to minimise loss and to resolve the dispute` IF
        g's `the court finds that an unfair practice has occurred`
    AND g's `the court is making an order in an action under section 6(1)`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(11)"
GIVEN g IS A `Regard Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must consider whether the consumer sought to resolve the dispute through the specified scheme` IF
        `the court must have regard to the consumer's efforts to minimise loss and to resolve the dispute` g
    AND g's `a specified dispute resolution scheme was available to the consumer in respect of the dispute`

-- 7(3) (subss 5(1)(b) and (2) to (5) of the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984 apply,
-- with modifications) and 7(6) (the Tribunal may make orders under that Act) point
-- into another Act and give this Act's rules no new condition: inert.

§§ `8. Voluntary compliance agreement`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(10) and (11), and s 2(1) 'specified body'"
GIVEN v IS A `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a specified body` IF
        v's `the body inviting the supplier is a person or body appointed by the Minister as a specified body`
    AND v's `the appointment has been published in the Gazette`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(1)"
GIVEN v IS A `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified body may invite the supplier to enter into a voluntary compliance agreement` IF
        `the body is a specified body` v
    AND v's `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice`

GIVEN u IS AN Undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking is not to engage in the unfair practice` IF
    CONSIDER u's `kind`
    WHEN `an undertaking that the supplier will not engage in the unfair practice` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN u IS AN Undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking is to compensate a consumer` IF
    CONSIDER u's `kind`
    WHEN `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN v IS A `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the voluntary compliance agreement satisfies section 8(2)` IF
        v's `the agreement is in writing`
    AND any (GIVEN u YIELD `the undertaking is not to engage in the unfair practice` u)
            (v's `the undertakings in the agreement`)

-- 8(3) and (4): an undertaking may be included, or the agreement varied to add or
-- vary one, with the supplier's agreement; 8(5): a compensation undertaking only at
-- the request of the consumer to whom it relates.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(3), (4) and (5)"
GIVEN u IS AN Undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking may be included or varied` IF
        u's `the supplier agrees to it`
    AND (IF `the undertaking is to compensate a consumer` u
         THEN u's `it is included in or varied in the agreement at the request of the consumer to whom it relates`
         ELSE TRUE)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(6)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Undertaking Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may recover the compensation as a civil debt` IF
        e's `the supplier has failed to comply with the undertaking`
    AND CONSIDER e's `the undertaking enforced`
        WHEN `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(7)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Undertaking Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified body may recover the reimbursement as a civil debt` IF
        e's `the supplier has failed to comply with the undertaking`
    AND CONSIDER e's `the undertaking enforced`
        WHEN `an undertaking to reimburse a specified body for costs or expenses incurred by it` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(8)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Undertaking Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified body may publicise the agreement and recover the costs as a civil debt` IF
        e's `the supplier has failed to comply with the undertaking`
    AND CONSIDER e's `the undertaking enforced`
        WHEN `an undertaking to publicise the voluntary compliance agreement` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(9)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Undertaking Enforcement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recovery bars all further actions to recover the loss, damage, costs or expenses to which the undertaking relates` IF
        e's `recovery under the agreement or under section 8(6), (7) or (8) has already been obtained`
    AND NOT e's `the agreement provides otherwise as to the bar on further actions`

§§ `9. Declaration or injunction`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is the District Court or the General Division of the High Court` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `the District Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the General Division of the High Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other court` THEN FALSE

-- 9(1) and (2): the power is on the Commission's application, exercisable if the
-- court is satisfied the supplier has engaged in the practice, whether or not it
-- intends to engage again, or that it is likely to engage in the absence of relief.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(1)(a), (b) and (2)"
GIVEN d IS A `Declaration Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` IF
        d's `the applicant is the Commission`
    AND `the court is the District Court or the General Division of the High Court` (d's `the court`)
    AND d's `the supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice`
    AND (   d's `the court is satisfied that the supplier has engaged in the unfair practice`
         OR d's `the court is satisfied that, if a declaration or an injunction is not granted, it is likely that the supplier will engage in the unfair practice`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(1)(c)"
GIVEN d IS A `Declaration Application Facts`
      `the court has granted relief under section 9(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make accompanying orders under section 9(4)` IF
        `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` d
    AND `the court has granted relief under section 9(1)(a) or (b)`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(3)"
GIVEN d IS A `Declaration Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant an interim injunction under section 9(3)` IF
        d's `the applicant is the Commission`
    AND `the court is the District Court or the General Division of the High Court` (d's `the court`)
    AND d's `the application for an injunction is pending determination`
    AND d's `the court considers an interim injunction desirable`

-- 9(4)(d): the duty to notify the Commission within 14 days.  The event must fall
-- "in a specified period"; whether it did is for the caller to establish before
-- arming the duty.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(4)(d)(i) to (ix)"
GIVEN event IS A `Business Change Event`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to an order` `Act under an order`
`the supplier's duty to notify the Commission of a business change event` MEANS
    PARTY `The supplier`
    MUST `notify the Commission in writing of a business change event` event
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The supplier` BECAUSE "the Commission was not notified in writing within 14 days after the event, as an order under section 9(4)(d) requires"

-- 9(4)(e) and (f): the Act says the individual must "inform the Commission in
-- writing if a notifiable event occurs in a specified period" and states no time.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(4)(e) and (f)"
GIVEN event IS A `Notifiable Event`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to an order` `Act under an order`
`the individual's duty to inform the Commission of a notifiable event` MEANS
    PARTY `The individual`
    MUST `inform the Commission in writing of a notifiable event` event
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The individual` BECAUSE "the Commission was not informed in writing of the notifiable event"

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10(6)(c)"
GIVEN event IS A `Notifiable Event`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to an order` `Act under an order`
`the injuncted individual's duty to inform the Commission of a notifiable event within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `The individual`
    MUST `inform the Commission in writing of a notifiable event` event
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The individual` BECAUSE "the Commission was not informed in writing within 14 days after the notifiable event, as an order under section 10(6)(c) requires"

-- 9(15) and the Fifth Schedule: "notifiable event" is an event specified in the
-- Fifth Schedule.  Each of paras 1 to 3 is an event as such; para 4 is an event
-- only at a holding of at least 15% of the total voting power or issued shares.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(15) and Fifth Schedule, paragraphs 1 to 4"
GIVEN e IS A `Notifiable Event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event is a notifiable event` IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the individual, as a sole proprietor, commences carrying on business as a supplier` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the individual is employed or ceases to be employed by a person who carries on a business as a supplier` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the individual becomes or ceases to be a director of a company which carries on a business as a supplier` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the individual becomes or ceases to be a partner in a partnership or limited partnership which carries on a business as a supplier` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the individual becomes or ceases to be a partner or manager of a limited liability partnership which carries on a business as a supplier` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the individual becomes or ceases to be interested in voting power or issued shares in a company which carries on a business as a supplier` pct THEN pct AT LEAST 15

-- 9(6): where two or more of the orders in (4)(a) to (d) are made, the specified
-- period in each must be the same.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(6)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Order Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified periods of the orders in section 9(4)(a) to (d) are the same` IF
    CONSIDER o's `the periods specified for the orders mentioned in section 9(4)(a), (b), (c) and (d), in years`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN all (GIVEN n YIELD n EQUALS first) rest

-- 9(7), 10(8): a specified period may not exceed 5 years, or the period the
-- Minister prescribes in its place.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(7) and s 10(8)"
GIVEN period IS A NUMBER
      `the period the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified period is within the ceiling of 5 years or the prescribed period` IF
    period AT MOST (CONSIDER `the period the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years`
                    WHEN JUST x THEN x
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN 5)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(7)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Order Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every specified period under section 9(4) is permitted` IF
        all (GIVEN n YIELD `the specified period is within the ceiling of 5 years or the prescribed period` n
                             (o's `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years`))
            (o's `the periods specified for the orders mentioned in section 9(4)(a), (b), (c) and (d), in years`)
    AND (CONSIDER o's `the period specified for an order mentioned in section 9(4)(e) or (f), in years`
         WHEN JUST n THEN `the specified period is within the ceiling of 5 years or the prescribed period` n (o's `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

-- 9(8), (9) and (10): on the Commission's application, where the supplier or
-- individual has failed to comply, the court may extend, but the aggregate of the
-- specified period and all extensions may not exceed 10 years after the date the
-- order was made, or the period the Minister prescribes in place of 10 years.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(8), (9) and (10)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Order Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may extend the specified period` IF
        o's `the Commission applies for the extension`
    AND o's `the supplier or individual has failed to comply with an order`
    AND o's `the aggregate in years of the specified period and all extensions`
        AT MOST (CONSIDER o's `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 10 years`
                 WHEN JUST x THEN x
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN 10)

-- 9(11), 10(10): a period prescribed by the Minister applies to an application made
-- on or after the date of the prescription.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(11) and s 10(10)"
GIVEN `the date on which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the date of the prescription` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prescribed period applies to the application` IF
    `the date on which the application is made` AT LEAST `the date of the prescription`

-- 9(12): the consumer may cancel within 6 months after the contract was entered
-- into.  The manner of cancellation and its effects are for regulations under
-- s 43(2)(m) (and s 11).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(12)"
GIVEN c IS A `Cancellation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer may cancel the contract` IF
        c's `the supplier entered into a consumer transaction in breach of an accompanying order to notify the consumer and obtain acknowledgment`
    AND c's `the date on which the consumer cancels`
        AT MOST `add months` (c's `the date on which the contract was entered into`) 6

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(12) and s 43(2)(m)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 43(2)(m) prescribing how a contract is cancelled under section 9(12) are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 43(2)(m) prescribing how a contract is cancelled under section 9(12) are encoded in this model"

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(14)"
GIVEN c IS A `Conclusive Proof Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is conclusive proof that the practice is an unfair practice` IF
        c's `the practice has been declared or permanently enjoined by the District Court or the General Division of the High Court as an unfair practice under section 9`
    AND c's `the proceedings are civil proceedings involving the supplier`
    AND NOT c's `the proceedings are an appeal from the order`

-- 9(5) (what "details" of a declaration or injunction include), 9(13) (subss (8),
-- (9) and (12) apply despite contempt proceedings): inert.

§§ `10. Injunction against a person knowingly abetting, aiding, permitting or procuring`

-- 10(2), 10(3) and 10(5) say that the power may be exercised "whether or not" the
-- person intends to continue, has abetted before, or irreparable harm is likely.
-- The rules take none of those as a condition, so those subsections are inert.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Abettor Injunction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant an injunction under section 10(1)` IF
        a's `the applicant is the Commission`
    AND `the court is the District Court or the General Division of the High Court` (a's `the court`)
    AND (   a's `the court is satisfied that the person has knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured the supplier to engage in the unfair practice`
         OR a's `the court is satisfied that, if an injunction is not granted, it is likely that the person will knowingly abet, aid, permit or procure the supplier to engage in the unfair practice`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10(4)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Abettor Injunction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant an interim injunction under section 10(4)` IF
        a's `the applicant is the Commission`
    AND `the court is the District Court or the General Division of the High Court` (a's `the court`)
    AND a's `the court considers an interim injunction desirable`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10(6)(c) and (8)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Abettor Injunction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the individual to inform the Commission of notifiable events for the specified period` IF
        `the court may grant an injunction under section 10(1)` a
    AND a's `the person is an individual`
    AND `the specified period is within the ceiling of 5 years or the prescribed period`
            (a's `the specified period in years`)
            (a's `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years`)

-- 10(9) and (10): if an individual fails to comply with an order under 10(6)(c), the
-- court may on the Commission's application extend the specified period to any time not
-- exceeding 10 years after the order was made, or the period the Minister prescribes in
-- place of 10 years.  The condition is the one in 9(8), (9) and (10); a prescribed period
-- applies to applications made on or after the date of prescription (10(10), the same
-- test as 9(11) above).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10(9) and (10)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Order Period Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may extend the specified period of the order under section 10(6)(c)` IF
    `the court may extend the specified period` o

§§ `11. Right to cancel certain contracts within cancellation period`

-- Section 11 is a power for the Minister to prescribe classes of cancellable
-- contracts and cancellation periods.  The section supplies no class and no period
-- of its own, so with no regulations as an input there is no answer.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 11(1) and (2)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 11 prescribing a class of cancellable contracts and a cancellation period are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 11 prescribing a class of cancellable contracts and a cancellation period are encoded in this model"

§§ `12. Limitation period`

-- 12(1)(b), (6), (7) and (8): the date on which the consumer first had knowledge.
-- The earliest of the date of actual knowledge and the date on which the consumer
-- might reasonably have been expected to acquire it from facts observable or
-- ascertainable by the consumer.  Knowledge from facts ascertainable only with
-- expert advice counts unless the consumer has taken all reasonable steps to obtain
-- and act on that advice (12(8)).  Whether the practice was unlawful is irrelevant
-- (12(6)); the facts record what the consumer knew of the facts.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earlier of two possible dates` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN (IF x LESS THAN y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12(1)(b), (7) and (8)"
GIVEN k IS A `Consumer Knowledge Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest date on which the consumer had knowledge` MEANS
    `the earlier of two possible dates`
        (`the earlier of two possible dates`
            (k's `the date on which the consumer actually had knowledge of the unfair practice`)
            (k's `the date on which the consumer might reasonably have been expected to acquire knowledge from facts observable or ascertainable by the consumer`))
        (IF k's `the consumer has taken all reasonable steps to obtain, and where appropriate to act on, that expert advice`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE k's `the date on which the consumer might reasonably have been expected to acquire knowledge from facts ascertainable with appropriate expert advice which it is reasonable to seek`)

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of a date and a possible date` MEANS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN JUST y THEN (IF y GREATER THAN a THEN y ELSE a)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN a

-- The date after which an action may not be commenced.  12(1), 12(3): two years
-- after the later of the last material event and (where there is one) the date of
-- knowledge.  12(2): one year after the failure to comply.  12(4): two years after
-- the last material event.  12(5): one year after cancellation.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12(1) to (5)"
GIVEN l IS A `Limitation Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for commencing the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER l's `kind of action`
    WHEN `an action under section 6` THEN
        `add months` (`the later of a date and a possible date`
                          (l's `the date of the occurrence of the last material event on which the action is based`)
                          (`the earliest date on which the consumer had knowledge` (l's `what the consumer knew`))) 24
    WHEN `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)` THEN
        `add months` (l's `the date of the failure to comply with the undertaking`) 12
    WHEN `an action under section 9` THEN
        `add months` (`the later of a date and a possible date`
                          (l's `the date of the occurrence of the last material event on which the action is based`)
                          (IF l's `the Commission alleges in the action an unfair practice in respect of a consumer`
                           THEN `the earliest date on which the consumer had knowledge` (l's `what the consumer knew`)
                           ELSE NOTHING)) 24
    WHEN `an action under section 10` THEN
        `add months` (l's `the date of the occurrence of the last material event on which the action is based`) 24
    WHEN `an action under regulations made under section 11` THEN
        `add months` (l's `the date of the cancellation of the contract`) 12

-- Fourth Schedule, paras 1 to 3: for an action under s 6, s 8(6) or regulations
-- made under s 11, the Limitation Act 1959 s 24(1) is replaced: a person under a
-- disability on the date the period begins may bring the action before the expiry of
-- one year after ceasing to be under a disability or dying, whichever first occurred,
-- even though the period has expired.  Para 4: ss 24A to 24C of that Act do not apply.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12(9) and Fourth Schedule, paragraphs 1 to 3"
GIVEN l IS A `Limitation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fourth Schedule extends the time for commencing the action` IF
        l's `the person to whom the action accrued was under a disability on the date after which the period of limitation begins to run`
    AND (CONSIDER l's `kind of action`
         WHEN `an action under section 6` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an action under regulations made under section 11` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (CONSIDER l's `the date on which that person ceased to be under a disability or died, whichever first occurred`
         WHEN JUST ended THEN l's `the date on which the action is commenced` AT MOST `add months` ended 12
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12(1) to (5) and Fourth Schedule"
GIVEN l IS A `Limitation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is commenced in time` IF
        l's `the date on which the action is commenced` AT MOST `the last day for commencing the action` l
     OR `the Fourth Schedule extends the time for commencing the action` l

-- 12(9), that the Limitation Act 1959 applies to these actions with the Fourth
-- Schedule's modifications, is the reason the Fourth Schedule is encoded above.
-- The rest of the Limitation Act 1959 is another Act and is not encoded.
